// Ω — the term that β-reduces to ITSELF, forever. `(λx. x x)(λx. x x)` steps to `(λx. x x)(λx. x x)`.
//
// The in-Rho driver is fuel-bounded, so it stops and SAYS SO on the ^drive-fuel channel, naming the
// redex it could not finish. Run-to-completion that cannot complete reports; it does not hang, and
// it does not quietly hand back a half-reduced term as if it were an answer.
//
// EXPECT   reduction fuel exhausted, stuck redex ⟦(λ.(0 0) λ.(0 0))⟧

lambda`(lam x. (x, x), lam x. (x, x))`
